\f0\fs24 \cf2 Look at this capital! A bust in armor, supported by two dolphins holding baskets of fruit. But there's a secret: its shape is inspired by a capital found in the sacristy of Santa Maria presso San Satiro in Milan, a masterpiece of Milanese Renaissance. And the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers? They didn\'92t just look, they copied with incredible precision. Every element that fascinated them during their travels was reproduced in the finest details, with perfect sketches that became actual plans for the craftsmen. Each decoration, like the one you see, isn\'92t just an embellishment, but a piece of history. And you, are you ready to uncover every hidden secret within these creations?}